// T4-E5 attempt (REQ-093's census, added 2026-09-17 before the deliverable ran; the spec's §7:
// an inexpressible claim ships with its failed attempt): a SCOPED FREEZE consulted on the
// indeterminate path (Feature 0.4 / W6 semantics). In our plane a freeze is a LATCHED state --
// once placed it holds every execute in its scope until it is released, and an execute whose
// evidence is indeterminate consults it; nothing about it is an event in the approval's own
// history. The nearest encoding is the open-session idiom over two posture events: "no Release
// since the last Freeze". Two things refuse it. (1) The language: `since` needs a `within`
// (the temporal grammar's `within_payload` is mandatory -- E6's physics), so a freeze older
// than the horizon is invisible and the latch has an expiry the plane's does not. (2) The
// vocabulary: the exported trace carries the five approval/execution actions only; a Freeze
// or a Release is the PLANE's posture, not an act in the trace, and the schema declares none --
// the kill-switch row (`T1-F5-kill-switch-001`) is this entry's driven exhibit: the pack
// ALLOWS because the trace carries nothing the freeze changed. The validator reports whichever
// it reaches first; the recorded output is the measurement.
@id("e5_scoped_freeze_latched_state")
forbid (principal, action == Req::Action::"Execute", resource)
when temporal {
    !Req::Action::"Release"::response{ input.scope: context.input.scope }
    since Req::Action::"Freeze"::response{ input.scope: context.input.scope }
};
